{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-49602" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that \n\n$$\n\\frac{2{x}^{2}-9x+13}{(x-3)^{2}(x+1)}=\\frac{A}{(x-3)}+\\frac{B}{(x-3)^{2}}+\\frac{C}{(x+1)},\n$$\n\nwhere $A$, $B$, and $C$ are real constants, determine the value of $A\\cdot B\\cdot C.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978241/state.json" "file_sha256" "f22d7a742285d7349a7a25f918cb2cd1e591ca801e1e0b8812588d2af6a15a75"} {"question" "q-49602" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Multiplying both sides of the given equality by $(x-3)^{2}(x+1)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}^{2}-9x+13 & =A(x-3)(x+1)+B(x+1)+C(x-3)^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=-1$  gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(-1)^{2}-9(-1)+13 & =A(-1-3)(-1+1)+B(-1+1)+C(-1-3)^{2} \\\\ 2+9+13 & =16C \\\\ 24 & =16C \\\\ C & =\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=3$  gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(3)^{2}-9(3)+13 & =A(3-3)(3+1)+B(3+1)+C(3-3)^{2} \\\\ 18-27+13 & =4B \\\\ 4 & =4B \\\\ B & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, letting $x=0$ and using our values for $B$ and $C$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(0)^{2}-9(0)+13 & =A(0-3)(0+1)+1(0+1)+\\frac{3}{2}(0-3)^{2} \\\\ 13 & =-3A+1+\\frac{27}{2} \\\\ 3A & =\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ A & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A\\cdot B\\cdot C & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 1\\cdot \\frac{3}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978241/state.json" "file_sha256" "f22d7a742285d7349a7a25f918cb2cd1e591ca801e1e0b8812588d2af6a15a75"} {"question" "q-49602" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978241/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c674f80e54f0fc7b89d9fa8bd5fa80b7fce4ccfebf386624558c79a78b1f23f1"} {"question" "q-49602" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978241/state.json" "file_sha256" "f22d7a742285d7349a7a25f918cb2cd1e591ca801e1e0b8812588d2af6a15a75"} {"question" "q-49602" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "4"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{9}"] ["math" "\\frac{7}{8}"] ["math" "\\frac{8}{3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978241/state.json" "file_sha256" "f22d7a742285d7349a7a25f918cb2cd1e591ca801e1e0b8812588d2af6a15a75"} {"question" "q-49602" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{3}{4}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978241/state.json" "file_sha256" "f22d7a742285d7349a7a25f918cb2cd1e591ca801e1e0b8812588d2af6a15a75"} {"question" "q-73385" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that \n\n$$\n\\frac{4x-1}{(x-3)^{3}}=\\frac{A}{x-3}+\\frac{B}{(x-3)^{2}}+\\frac{C}{(x-3)^{3}},\n$$\n\nwhere $A$, $B$ and $C$ are real constants, find the value of $A\\cdot B\\cdot C.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978241/state.json" "file_sha256" "f22d7a742285d7349a7a25f918cb2cd1e591ca801e1e0b8812588d2af6a15a75"} {"question" "q-73385" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Multiplying both sides of the given equality by $(x-3)^{3}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x-1 & =A(x-3)^{2}+B(x-3)+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=3$  gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(3)-1 & =A(3-3)^{2}+B(3-3)+C \\\\ 11 & =A(0)+B(0)+C \\\\ C & =11.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=0$ and using our value for $C$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(0)-1 & =A(0-3)^{2}+B(0-3)+11 \\\\ -1 & =9A-3B+11 \\\\ 0 & =9A-3B+12 \\\\ 0 & =3A-B+4 \\\\ B & =3A+4.\\,\\,(1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, letting $x=2$ and using our value for $C$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(2)-1 & =A(2-3)^{2}+B(2-3)+11 \\\\ 7 & =A-B+11 \\\\ 0 & =A-B+4 \\\\ B & =4+A.\\,\\,(2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom $(1)$ and $(2)$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3A+4 & =4+A \\\\ 2A & =0 \\\\ A & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we substitute the value of $A$ into $(2)$  to get the value of $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B & =4+0=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A\\cdot B\\cdot C & =0\\cdot 4\\cdot 11=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978241/state.json" "file_sha256" "f22d7a742285d7349a7a25f918cb2cd1e591ca801e1e0b8812588d2af6a15a75"} {"question" "q-73385" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978241/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c674f80e54f0fc7b89d9fa8bd5fa80b7fce4ccfebf386624558c79a78b1f23f1"} {"question" "q-73385" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978241/state.json" "file_sha256" "f22d7a742285d7349a7a25f918cb2cd1e591ca801e1e0b8812588d2af6a15a75"} {"question" "q-73385" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-10"] ["math" "-8"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "12"] ["math" "9"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978241/state.json" "file_sha256" "f22d7a742285d7349a7a25f918cb2cd1e591ca801e1e0b8812588d2af6a15a75"} {"question" "q-73385" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978241/state.json" "file_sha256" "f22d7a742285d7349a7a25f918cb2cd1e591ca801e1e0b8812588d2af6a15a75"} {"question" "q-351184" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Express $\\frac{3x+2}{(x-7)^{2}}$ as a sum of partial fractions.\n\n|  | $\\frac{3x+2}{(x-7)^{2}}\\,=\\,\\frac{3}{(x-7)}\\,\\,+$ | {{field-1}} |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | $(x-7)^{2}$ |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978241/state.json" "file_sha256" "f22d7a742285d7349a7a25f918cb2cd1e591ca801e1e0b8812588d2af6a15a75"} {"question" "q-351184" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Our task is to find $B$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3x+2}{(x-7)^{2}}=\\frac{3}{(x-7)}+\\frac{B}{(x-7)^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by $(x-7)^{2}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x+2 & =3(x-7)+B.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=7$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(7)+2 & =3(7-7)+B \\\\ 21+2 & =0+B \\\\ B & =23.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\frac{3x+2}{(x-7)^{2}}=\\frac{3}{(x-7)}+\\frac{23}{(x-7)^{2}}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978241/state.json" "file_sha256" "f22d7a742285d7349a7a25f918cb2cd1e591ca801e1e0b8812588d2af6a15a75"} {"question" "q-351184" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978241/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c674f80e54f0fc7b89d9fa8bd5fa80b7fce4ccfebf386624558c79a78b1f23f1"} {"question" "q-351184" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978241/state.json" "file_sha256" "f22d7a742285d7349a7a25f918cb2cd1e591ca801e1e0b8812588d2af6a15a75"} {"question" "q-351184" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "23"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978241/state.json" "file_sha256" "f22d7a742285d7349a7a25f918cb2cd1e591ca801e1e0b8812588d2af6a15a75"} {"question" "q-351199" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Express $\\frac{6x-11}{(x-4)^{2}}$ as a sum of partial fractions.\n\n| $\\frac{6x-11}{(x-4)^{2}}=$ | {{field-1}} | $+$ | {{field-2}} |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $x-4$ |  | $(x-4)^{2}$ |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978241/state.json" "file_sha256" "f22d7a742285d7349a7a25f918cb2cd1e591ca801e1e0b8812588d2af6a15a75"} {"question" "q-351199" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Our task is to find $A$ and $B$ such that\n\n$$\n\\frac{6x-11}{(x-4)^{2}}=\\frac{A}{x-4}+\\frac{B}{(x-4)^{2}}.\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the given equality by $(x-4)^{2}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6x-11 & =A(x-4)+B.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=4$  gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6(4)-11 & =A(4-4)+B \\\\ 13 & =B.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=0$ and using our value for $B$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6(0)-11 & =A(0-4)+13 \\\\ -11 & =-4A+13 \\\\ -4A & =-24 \\\\ A & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\frac{6x-11}{(x-4)^{2}}=\\frac{6}{x-4}+\\frac{13}{(x-4)^{2}}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978241/state.json" "file_sha256" "f22d7a742285d7349a7a25f918cb2cd1e591ca801e1e0b8812588d2af6a15a75"} {"question" "q-351199" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978241/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c674f80e54f0fc7b89d9fa8bd5fa80b7fce4ccfebf386624558c79a78b1f23f1"} {"question" "q-351199" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978241/state.json" "file_sha256" "f22d7a742285d7349a7a25f918cb2cd1e591ca801e1e0b8812588d2af6a15a75"} {"question" "q-351199" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "6"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978241/state.json" "file_sha256" "f22d7a742285d7349a7a25f918cb2cd1e591ca801e1e0b8812588d2af6a15a75"} {"question" "q-351199" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978241/state.json" "file_sha256" "f22d7a742285d7349a7a25f918cb2cd1e591ca801e1e0b8812588d2af6a15a75"} {"question" "q-351199" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "13"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978241/state.json" "file_sha256" "f22d7a742285d7349a7a25f918cb2cd1e591ca801e1e0b8812588d2af6a15a75"} {"question" "q-351200" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Express $\\frac{2x-9}{(x-3)^{2}}$ as a sum of partial fractions.\n\n| $\\frac{2x-9}{(x-3)^{2}}=$ | {{field-1}} | $-$ | {{field-2}} |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $x-3$ |  | $(x-3)^{2}$ |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978241/state.json" "file_sha256" "f22d7a742285d7349a7a25f918cb2cd1e591ca801e1e0b8812588d2af6a15a75"} {"question" "q-351200" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Our task is to find $A$ and $B$ such that\n\n$$\n\\frac{2x-9}{(x-3)^{2}}=\\frac{A}{x-3}+\\frac{B}{(x-3)^{2}}.\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the given equality by $(x-3)^{2}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-9 & =A(x-3)+B.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=3$  gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(3)-9 & =A(3-3)+B \\\\ -3 & =B.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=0$ and using our value for $B$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(0)-9 & =A(0-3)-3 \\\\ -9 & =-3A-3 \\\\ -3A & =-6 \\\\ A & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\frac{2x-9}{(x-3)^{2}}=\\frac{2}{x-3}-\\frac{3}{(x-3)^{2}}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978241/state.json" "file_sha256" "f22d7a742285d7349a7a25f918cb2cd1e591ca801e1e0b8812588d2af6a15a75"} {"question" "q-351200" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978241/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c674f80e54f0fc7b89d9fa8bd5fa80b7fce4ccfebf386624558c79a78b1f23f1"} {"question" "q-351200" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978241/state.json" "file_sha256" "f22d7a742285d7349a7a25f918cb2cd1e591ca801e1e0b8812588d2af6a15a75"} {"question" "q-351200" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978241/state.json" "file_sha256" "f22d7a742285d7349a7a25f918cb2cd1e591ca801e1e0b8812588d2af6a15a75"} {"question" "q-351200" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978241/state.json" "file_sha256" "f22d7a742285d7349a7a25f918cb2cd1e591ca801e1e0b8812588d2af